---
description: Rules for demo data, editorial content and future Supabase integration.
globs: ["**/data/**", "**/content/**", "**/features/**", "**/lib/**", "**/supabase/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---
- Start with realistic but clearly fictional/demo data.
- Never invent claims about the future real client.
- Define domain models before database tables.
- Public pages should depend on repository interfaces, not directly on Supabase queries.
- Events need status, publication state, date/time, venue, location, pricing text, description, image/media references and optional registration/contact information.
- Preserve room for recurring events and multiple class sessions without prematurely over-modeling.
- Editorial content should support title, excerpt, body, hero media, taxonomy, publication date, author/byline and SEO metadata.
- When real content is introduced later, replace demo records without redesigning the page architecture.
